 "method": "Bounded, finite, deterministic Pass C test for Goro_Goro_and_Satoru (requested: exact approved baseline vs the two Bitterblossom\ncut alternatives, same source assumptions/opponents, paid turn-three UBR, turn 3-7 resource/card draw, blockers/flyers, commander removal,\nsweepers, one realistic extra-combat window). NOT a game simulation and NOT a win-rate: every cell is one fully scripted line resolved by\nhand-coded rules. Shared script (identical for every variant): on the play, mana available on turn t = t (land drop every turn, no rocks);\nT1 Slither Blade (1/2 unblockable); T3 Goro-Goro and Satoru paid {U}{B}{R}; Goro never attacks. Goro rules: one Dragon Spirit 5/5 flier\nper player dealt combat damage by >=1 creature that entered this turn (CR 603.2c one trigger per damage event per player); {1}{R} haste\naffects only creatures on the battlefield at resolution (CR 611.2c), so Dragons made in combat 1 need a second activation for combat 2.\nTested card X is the ONLY variable: Bitterblossom (cast T2), Bident of Thassa (cast T4), Grazilaxx, Illithid Scholar (cast T4),\nMist-Syndicate Naga (ninjutsu {2}{U} T4 returning Slither Blade, which is recast for {U} the next turn), Redoubled Stormsinger (cast T4,\nattacks from T5). Board profiles: lean (Slither Blade only) and engine (adds Daring Piracy already on board from T4: a fresh 1/1 menace\nhaste Pirate each combat). Opponent configs: open (no relevant blockers); flyer_wall (one untapped 2/2 flier that blocks the best\nnon-unblockable fresh attacker each combat); removal (Goro destroyed at start of T5, recast T6 with tax); sweeper (all creatures die at start\nof T6, Goro recast T7 with tax); extra (Great Train Heist {R} on T6: one additional combat; second haste activation paid if mana allows).\nFresh connecters are assumed to be spread across up to three opponents (Dragons = min(fresh connecters, 3)); non-fresh attackers go to one\nopponent. Bident draws per connecting creature; Grazilaxx draws per player dealt damage and returns a blocked attacker to hand.",
